PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The deliberation remains divided between Choice D and Choice B regarding whether the classic sterol-sparing effect rescues development to adulthood. Under physiological principles established in the literature, bulk dietary cholestanol satisfies structural membrane requirements, leaving catalytic precursor needs to be met either by maternal carryover (Scenario 1) or trace dietary supplementation (Scenario 2). Additionally, the textual reference to reproducing mothers in Scenario 2 logically necessitates successful adult eclosion in Scenario 1. Therefore, both experimental conditions result in complete development, directly supporting Choice D as the correct answer.
}

